# Task 156-009 Plan — assertSpawnSafe Whitelist Runtime

## Goal
Defansif spawn safety primitivi olusturmak. spawn-backend-docker.ts ve gelecekteki adapter cagrilari oncesi cagrilacak.

## Files (within scope)
- src/core/spawn-safety.ts (new)
- tests/core/spawn-safety.test.ts (new)

## Out-of-scope (cannot modify in this task)
- src/orchestra/spawn-backend-docker.ts — outside src/core/ scope.
  Wire-up will be flagged as follow-up in result. The module is exported and ready to import.

## Design
### Public API
- `ADAPTER_BIN_WHITELIST: readonly string[]` — frozen list of allowed binaries
  ['node','npx','vitest','tsc','python','python3','go','cargo','java','dotnet']
- `SH_C_ALLOWED: RegExp` — `/^[A-Za-z0-9_\-\.\/\s\=]+$/`
- `class SpawnSafetyError extends Error` with codes:
  - BIN_NOT_WHITELISTED
  - ARG_INJECTION
  - INVALID_INPUT
- `assertSpawnSafe(bin: string, args: string[], opts?): void` — throws on violation
- `isSpawnSafe(bin, args, opts?): boolean` — boolean wrapper for convenience

### Validation logic
1. Input shape: bin = non-empty string, args = string[]
2. bin: extract basename (handles `/usr/bin/node`), check membership in whitelist
3. args: each non-empty arg must match SH_C_ALLOWED (allows alnum, `_-./\s=`)
   - Empty args allowed (no injection vector)
4. opts.binWhitelist override for tests/specialized adapters

### Test cases (>= 14)
- rm rejected (not whitelisted)
- npx vitest run accepted
- Inline `;` injection arg rejected
- `&&`, `|`, backtick, `$()`, `<`, `>`, newline rejected
- Whole whitelist accepted with minimal args
- Absolute path bin (`/usr/bin/node`) accepted via basename
- Empty args array accepted
- Non-string bin / non-array args → INVALID_INPUT
- SpawnSafetyError shape: code/bin/badArg fields
- isSpawnSafe boolean variant
- Custom whitelist override
- ADAPTER_BIN_WHITELIST is frozen (mutation throws)
- SH_C_ALLOWED regex independently exported & matches expected

